PodMotion eBPF Programs (bpf/)
License: GPL-2.0 OR BSD-2-Clause (pm_relay.c, pm_xdp_vtep.c, zero_window.c, xdp_bridge.c)
         GPL-2.0-only              (pm_sk_lookup.c — uses bpf_sk_assign, a GPL-only kernel helper)

The following compiled eBPF object files are embedded into the pm-agent binary at
build time via //go:embed directives in internal/agent/network/bpfloader/:

  pm_relay_bpfel.o       — GPL-2.0 OR BSD-2-Clause
  pm_xdp_vtep_bpfel.o    — GPL-2.0 OR BSD-2-Clause
  pm_sk_lookup_bpfel.o   — GPL-2.0-only (bpf_sk_assign kernel helper is GPL-only)
  zero_window_bpfel.o    — GPL-2.0 OR BSD-2-Clause
  zero_window_bpfeb.o    — GPL-2.0 OR BSD-2-Clause

These objects are BPF bytecode that runs in the Linux kernel context, not in
userspace.  The GPL-2.0-only object (pm_sk_lookup_bpfel.o) is isolated in a
separate ELF section and its GPL license obligation applies to the eBPF bytecode
itself and any kernel modules that link it, not to the Apache-2.0 userspace Go
binary that loads and manages it via the bpf(2) syscall (BPF program loading via
syscall does not constitute static linking for GPL copyleft purposes).

Downstream redistributors who modify the eBPF C sources must satisfy the
GPL-2.0 obligations for any modified pm_sk_lookup.c-derived objects, and
BSD-2-Clause or GPL-2.0 obligations for objects derived from the other files.

